From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] do not rearm monitor timer after synchronous stop

The monitor polling callback rearmed its QDF timer unconditionally at its
exit. A concurrent qdf_timer_sync_cancel could clear MON_VDEV_TIMER_RUNNING
while the callback was executing, after which the callback requeued itself and
touched monitor state during delayed vdev teardown. Check the running bit at
the rearm point. This is limited to timer lifecycle; no RX/TX format or
firmware behavior changes.

--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_1.0.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_1.0.c
@@ -534,6 +534,11 @@
 	}
 
 budget_done:
+	/* A synchronous stop can race with the callback already executing.
+	 * Do not re-arm after the stop cleared RUNNING; otherwise a delayed
+	 * monitor teardown leaves this callback touching freed monitor state. */
+	if (!(mon_soc->mon_vdev_timer_state & MON_VDEV_TIMER_RUNNING))
+		return;
 	if (yield == DP_TIMER_WORK_EXHAUST ||
 	    yield == DP_TIMER_TIME_EXHAUST)
 		qdf_timer_mod(&mon_soc->mon_vdev_timer, 1);
